        "displayName": "Protractor Cucumber",
        "readme": "<p>This module demonstrates how Serenity/JS integrates with the legacy Protractor framework using Cucumber.js as the test runner.</p>\n<h2>Why this module?</h2>\n<p>Protractor has been deprecated, but Serenity/JS continues to support it to help teams migrate to Playwright or WebdriverIO at their own pace. The Screenplay Pattern abstractions remain portable across all supported tools.</p>\n<h2>Features demonstrated</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Passing scenario reporting through Protractor&#39;s Cucumber integration</li>\n<li>Filtering Cucumber scenarios by line number</li>\n<li>Native Cucumber formatter support alongside Serenity/JS reporting</li>\n<li>Gherkin scenarios executed via Protractor with Angular-aware browser automation</li>\n</ul>\n"
